o resolve through node1. Implementation is a two-play Ansible playbook (/root/ansible-dns/playbook.yml on node4): play 1 uses raw VyOS configure-mode commands (wrapped in sudo bash -c, required because Ubuntu 16.04/VyOS lack a python3 new enough for standard ansible-core 2.21 modules) to set service dns forwarding + static-host-mapping and verifies local resolution; play 2 uses raw SSH commands to install /etc/resolvconf/resolv.conf.d/head with nameserver 10.100.232.10, regenerate resolv.conf, and verify both inventory.internal and a public name resolve. Verified idempotent re-runs. Completed the mandatory restart-evidence protocol: captured healthy baselines, restarted node1, node2, node3, node4 one at a time (native reboot), confirmed each node's boot_id changed, and confirmed DNS forwarding/config persistence and client resolution recovered on every node, including a full successful Ansible playbook re-run from node4 after its own reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed all 4 nodes: node1=VyOS router (DNS target), node2/node3=Ubuntu 16.04 (DNS clients), node4=Ubuntu 24.04 control node with ansible-core 2.21 pre-installed, all on shared 10.100.232.0/24\",\"Set up passwordless SSH from node4 to node1 (vyos user, added via VyOS system login public-keys), node2 and node3 (antrieb user, appended cluster pubkey to authorized_keys)\",\"Manually validated the exact VyOS DNS forwarding + static-host-mapping command sequence before automating it\",\"Wrote Ansible inventory.ini, ansible.cfg, and playbook.yml on node4 under /root/ansible-dns\",\"Diagnosed and fixed 'set -e' + pty interaction causing false failures on VyOS raw commands\",\"Diagnosed and fixed ansible-core module f-string incompatibility with Ubuntu 16.04's Python 3.5.2 by switching client tasks to ansible.builtin.raw\",\"Ran the playbook end-to-end, verified inventory.internal resolves to 10.100.232.11 and public names resolve via forwarding, from node1 and from node2/node3\",\"Re-ran the playbook to confirm idempotency\",\"Captured boot_id/service/data baselines on all 4 nodes\",\"Restarted node1, node2, node3, node4 sequentially via native reboot, polling each until reachable again\",\"Confirmed changed boot_id on every node post-restart\",\"Verified DNS forwarding config, static-host-mapping, and client resolv.conf/resolution all persisted and recovered after each restart, and re-ran the full Ansible playbook successfully from node4 after its own reboot\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1 configured as DNS forwarder answering inventory.internal with node2's address and forwarding everything else upstream\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-17d7c20f5f8c469b\",\"cmd-80215e19446840bc\",\"cmd-13bbd69976c54166\"],\"summary\":\"VyOS service dns forwarding + static-host-mapping applied and committed/saved via Ansible; dig confirms inventory.internal -> 10.100.232.11 and example.com resolves via upstream 10.100.232.1\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 configured to resolve through node1, implemented via Ansible\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-13bbd69976c54166\",\"cmd-4008b74dea8346b6\"],\"summary\":\"Ansible playbook run installs resolvconf head file pointing at 10.100.232.10 on both clients; getent hosts confirms inventory.internal and example.com resolve correctly through node1\"},{\"requirement\":\"Implementation performed via Ansible from the designated control node\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-afa17fff762f41d6\",\"cmd-13bbd69976c54166\",\"cmd-4008b74dea8346b6\"],\"summary\":\"inventory.ini/ansible.cfg/playbook.yml created on node4 (control_node) and ansible-playbook executed from there against node1/node2/node3\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered DNS state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1a5e49c03bad42c0\",\"cmd-b1b6125519ca48e8\",\"cmd-1674728b796c40df\",\"cmd-44bcf48e207440e4\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 5bcff8f9...; reboot issued; post-reboot boot_id changed to 7bc5f980...; DNS forwarding config, static-host-mapping and resolution all confirmed working after restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered client DNS resolution\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6f4979fbeb814b84\",\"cmd-9ccfd46a8b7142f6\",\"cmd-368ebe4ed1d04131\",\"cmd-f501256393354695\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 2dffe735...; reboot issued; post-reboot boot_id changed to 780db765...; resolv.conf and inventory.internal/example.com resolution confirmed recovered\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered client DNS resolution\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-202eacd1315e4398\",\"cmd-920b37a68b7244a6\",\"cmd-a1ded998e60e4694\",\"cmd-912bce5e3e2b42fd\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id dbb46974...; reboot issued; post-reboot boot_id changed to 81c263fd...; resolv.conf and resolution confirmed recovered\"},{\"requirement\":\"node4 (control node) restart baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered orchestration capability\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d60ef54c87cb476c\",\"cmd-065ae67192f7430c\",\"cmd-24a15977601441b5\",\"cmd-1d3caeaade2b4cbd\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id d3d54083...; reboot issued; post-reboot boot_id changed to e114543b...; full Ansible playbook re-run from node4 succeeded end-to-end after its own restart, proving orchestration capability recovered\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 (VyOS) as the DNS forwarder for the shared 10.100.232.0/24 network using Ansible from control node node4. node1 answers inventory.internal with node2's address (10.100.232.11) via a VyOS static-host-mapping and forwards all other queries to the upstream resolver 10.100.232.1. node2 and node3 (Ubuntu 16.04) are configured via a resolvconf head override to resolve through node1. Implementation is a two-play Ansible playbook (/root/ansible-dns/playbook.yml on node4): play 1 uses raw VyOS configure-mode commands (wrapped in sudo bash -c, required because Ubuntu 16.04/VyOS lack a python3 new enough for standard ansible-core 2.21 modules) to set service dns forwarding + static-host-mapping and verifies local resolution; play 2 uses raw SSH commands to install /etc/resolvconf/resolv.conf.d/head with nameserver 10.100.232.10, regenerate resolv.conf, and verify both inventory.internal and a public name resolve. Verified idempotent re-runs. Completed the mandatory restart-evidence protocol: captured healthy baselines, restarted node1, node2, node3, node4 one at a time (native reboot), confirmed each node's boot_id changed, and confirmed DNS forwarding/config persistence and client resolution recovered on every node, including a full successful Ansible playbook re-run from node4 after its own reboot.","actions_performed":["Surveyed all 4 nodes: node1=VyOS router (DNS target), node2/node3=Ubuntu 16.04 (DNS clients), node4=Ubuntu 24.04 control node with ansible-core 2.21 pre-installed, all on shared 10.100.232.0/24","Set up passwordless SSH from node4 to node1 (vyos user, added via VyOS system login public-keys), node2 and node3 (antrieb user, appended cluster pubkey to authorized_keys)","Manually validated the exact VyOS DNS forwarding + static-host-mapping command sequence before automating it","Wrote Ansible inventory.ini, ansible.cfg, and playbook.yml on node4 under /root/ansible-dns","Diagnosed and fixed 'set -e' + pty interaction causing false failures on VyOS raw commands","Diagnosed and fixed ansible-core module f-string incompatibility with Ubuntu 16.04's Python 3.5.2 by switching client tasks to ansible.builtin.raw","Ran the playbook end-to-end, verified inventory.internal resolves to 10.100.232.11 and public names resolve via forwarding, from node1 and from node2/node3","Re-ran the playbook to confirm idempotency","Captured boot_id/service/data baselines on all 4 nodes","Restarted node1, node2, node3, node4 sequentially via native reboot, polling each until reachable again","Confirmed changed boot_id on every node post-restart","Verified DNS forwarding config, static-host-mapping, and client resolv.conf/resolution all persisted and recovered after each restart, and re-ran the full Ansible playbook successfully from node4 after its own reboot"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1 configured as DNS forwarder answering inventory.internal with node2's address and forwarding everything else upstream","command_ids":["cmd-17d7c20f5f8c469b","cmd-80215e19446840bc","cmd-13bbd69976c54166"],"summary":"VyOS service dns forwarding + static-host-mapping applied and committed/saved via Ansible; dig confirms inventory.internal -> 10.100.232.11 and example.com resolves via upstream 10.100.232.1"},{"requirement":"node2 and node3 configured to resolve through node1, implemented via Ansible","command_ids":["cmd-13bbd69976c54166","cmd-4008b74dea8346b6"],"summary":"Ansible playbook run installs resolvconf head file pointing at 10.100.232.10 on both clients; getent hosts confirms inventory.internal and example.com resolve correctly through node1"},{"requirement":"Implementation performed via Ansible from the designated control node","command_ids":["cmd-afa17fff762f41d6","cmd-13bbd69976c54166","cmd-4008b74dea8346b6"],"summary":"inventory.ini/ansible.cfg/playbook.yml created on node4 (control_node) and ansible-playbook executed from there against node1/node2/node3"},{"requirement":"node1 restart baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered DNS state","command_ids":["cmd-1a5e49c03bad42c0","cmd-b1b6125519ca48e8","cmd-1674728b796c40df","cmd-44bcf48e207440e4"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 5bcff8f9...; reboot issued; post-reboot boot_id changed to 7bc5f980...; DNS forwarding config, static-host-mapping and resolution all confirmed working after restart"},{"requirement":"node2 restart baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered client DNS resolution","command_ids":["cmd-6f4979fbeb814b84","cmd-9ccfd46a8b7142f6","cmd-368ebe4ed1d04131","cmd-f501256393354695"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 2dffe735...; reboot issued; post-reboot boot_id changed to 780db765